            "description": "\n.. image:: https://badge.fury.io/py/kaiju-redis.svg\n    :target: https://pypi.org/project/kaiju-redis\n    :alt: Latest package version\n\n.. image:: https://readthedocs.org/projects/kaiju-redis/badge/?version=latest\n    :target: https://kaiju-redis.readthedocs.io/en/latest/?badge=latest\n    :alt: Documentation Status\n\nSummary\n-------\n\n**Python**: >=3.8\n\n`Project documentation <https://kaiju-redis.readthedocs.io/en/latest/>`_\n\nRedis / keydb services (cache, streams, locks).\n\nUse `pip install kaiju-redis` to install the package.\n\nFor development run the init script `tools/init.sh`.\nIt will setup git hooks and install the dev version of the project.\n\nTesting\n_______\n\n- Install additional dependencies `pip install -e .[dev]`\n- Start docker daemon.\n- Run `pytest` from the project root.\n\nDocumentation\n_____________\n\n- Install additional dependencies `pip install -e .[docs]`\n- Run `docs/docs.sh` from the project root to generate documentation.\n",
